1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:05,635
In Lagos, an importer sends a thirty percent deposit to a supplier in Shenzhen.

2
00:00:05,935 --> 00:00:08,590
The seventy percent balance is where it goes wrong.

3
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:12,538
Goods that never arrive. Over three billion dollars lost

4
00:00:12,538 --> 00:00:16,186
in 2025 to "our bank details have changed" scams.

5
00:00:16,486 --> 00:00:19,366
A naira that lost a third of its value in

6
00:00:19,366 --> 00:00:22,246
a single day. And letters of credit have almost vanished.

7
00:00:22,546 --> 00:00:26,405
Arra is Latin for earnest money: the deposit that secures a deal.

8
00:00:26,705 --> 00:00:31,014
Pay the deposit, and keep the balance locked in an open contract on Celo.

9
00:00:31,314 --> 00:00:35,754
Before any order, paste the page you found your supplier on. Arra's agent pays

10
00:00:35,754 --> 00:00:40,512
half a cent per lookup to read it, and searches X and Reddit for complaints.

11
00:00:40,812 --> 00:00:44,446
This example shop has two customer complaints: high risk.

12
00:00:45,371 --> 00:00:48,353
A real seller comes back green. And suppliers

13
00:00:48,353 --> 00:00:51,707
can confirm their own page, so impersonators get flagged.

14
00:00:53,293 --> 00:00:57,240
Describe the order like a message, and the assistant fills in the terms.

15
00:00:59,507 --> 00:01:02,258
Vague words like "good quality" are refused, and

16
00:01:02,258 --> 00:01:05,352
the terms are fingerprinted, so they can't change later.

17
00:01:05,652 --> 00:01:08,522
Send your supplier one link. They read the terms

18
00:01:08,522 --> 00:01:11,711
in English or Chinese, and agree from their own wallet.

19
00:01:13,722 --> 00:01:15,898
You see their record and reviews, and

20
00:01:15,898 --> 00:01:18,385
a changed payout address sets off an alarm.

21
00:01:18,685 --> 00:01:22,492
Pay from the wallet you already use: MiniPay, MetaMask, Rabby,

22
00:01:22,492 --> 00:01:26,680
or any wallet on Celo. In dollars, or straight from naira.

23
00:01:26,980 --> 00:01:29,694
Lock the order. The supplier accepts, and

24
00:01:29,694 --> 00:01:32,796
the deposit reaches them instantly. The balance waits.

25
00:01:35,042 --> 00:01:38,968
Every naira payment is a Textile FX fill: one firm

26
00:01:38,968 --> 00:01:42,893
quote for exactly the dollars needed, settled in one transaction.

27
00:01:43,193 --> 00:01:47,110
That one rate matters. In 2023, a seven-thousand-dollar balance

28
00:01:47,110 --> 00:01:51,027
cost two million naira more, just seven weeks later.

29
00:01:51,327 --> 00:01:53,365
With Arra, it's paid for on day one.

30
00:01:53,665 --> 00:01:56,017
When they ship, the container number is checked,

31
00:01:56,017 --> 00:01:58,664
and your check period starts when the goods arrive.

32
00:02:00,491 --> 00:02:03,460
All good? Pay the balance in one tap, or in parts.

33
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:07,234
Something wrong? Report it with signed photos, and make an offer.

34
00:02:07,534 --> 00:02:10,439
Cancel before they accept. No accept, or

35
00:02:10,439 --> 00:02:13,760
no shipment, and Arra's agent refunds you automatically.

36
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:18,198
A quiet buyer can't hold the money: ignored offers go through in

37
00:02:18,198 --> 00:02:22,337
seven days. And nobody, not even Arra, can send it anywhere else.

38
00:02:22,637 --> 00:02:26,017
Afterwards, both sides review each other, hidden until both

39
00:02:26,017 --> 00:02:29,397
have written. Receipts and history stay with every order.

40
00:02:31,362 --> 00:02:34,828
It works for any deposit-and-balance deal: a house built

41
00:02:34,828 --> 00:02:38,295
back home, furniture made to order, a freelance project.

42
00:02:38,595 --> 00:02:43,331
Arra is live on Celo mainnet. A friend's real order ran start to finish.

43
00:02:43,631 --> 00:02:47,045
Verified contract, a registered agent, naira filled

44
00:02:47,045 --> 00:02:50,947
through Textile, and supplier checks paid over x402.

45
00:02:51,647 --> 00:02:53,839
Arra. Trade with anyone, without the worry.
